WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.461
Secure uploads begin with a narrow
contract for the feature.

2
00:00:04.461 --> 00:00:06.913
Specify allowed formats, file counts,
actual

3
00:00:06.913 --> 00:00:09.553
byte limits, retention, and replacement
behavior.

4
00:00:09.553 --> 00:00:13.420
Authorize the caller against the intended
resource and tenant, then

5
00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:17.381
keep that ownership attached to a server
controlled storage record.

6
00:00:17.381 --> 00:00:20.493
Authentication does not validate file
contents, and successful

7
00:00:20.493 --> 00:00:23.699
file validation does not authorize upload
or retrieval.

8
00:00:23.699 --> 00:00:26.057
TypeScript can describe the contract, but

9
00:00:26.057 --> 00:00:28.132
runtime components must enforce it.

10
00:00:28.132 --> 00:00:32.281
Treat filenames, extensions, and declared
media types as untrusted metadata.

11
00:00:32.281 --> 00:00:35.016
An extension is not file identity, and

12
00:00:35.016 --> 00:00:37.845
a declared type is not verified
classification.

13
00:00:37.845 --> 00:00:40.108
Generate storage names instead of relying

14
00:00:40.108 --> 00:00:42.560
on filename cleanup to control
destinations.

15
00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:46.050
Keep local paths under trusted roots, own
bucket and

16
00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:49.728
key selection on the server, and prevent
accidental overwrites.

17
00:00:49.728 --> 00:00:52.745
Restrict temporary storage and clean up
failed work

18
00:00:52.745 --> 00:00:55.952
with the same care used for permanent
objects.

19
00:00:55.952 --> 00:00:59.724
Combine content recognition, intended
parser checks, and structural policy.

20
00:00:59.724 --> 00:01:02.742
Re-encode selected media when a controlled
output meaningfully

21
00:01:02.742 --> 00:01:05.665
reduces retained complexity, without
claiming universal sanitization.

22
00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:07.551
Store content away from application

23
00:01:07.551 --> 00:01:09.626
code and automatic public interpretation.

24
00:01:09.626 --> 00:01:12.644
Bound decompressed data, pixels, pages,
processing time,

25
00:01:12.644 --> 00:01:15.473
and generated output separately from
request size.

26
00:01:15.473 --> 00:01:17.737
Maintain complex parsers and isolate
higher

27
00:01:17.737 --> 00:01:19.811
risk processing with least privilege.

28
00:01:19.811 --> 00:01:23.489
Sandboxing limits consequences; it does
not replace input validation.

29
00:01:23.489 --> 00:01:26.884
Scanning and quarantine add useful
controls when the workflow

30
00:01:26.884 --> 00:01:30.562
warrants them, but scanning is not proof
of safety.

31
00:01:30.562 --> 00:01:34.146
Promote only the exact object whose
required checks passed.

32
00:01:34.146 --> 00:01:37.729
At download time, authorize access and
select content type,

33
00:01:37.729 --> 00:01:41.502
disposition, caching, and origin policy
for the intended use.

34
00:01:41.502 --> 00:01:44.708
Safe storage does not imply safe inline
rendering.

35
00:01:44.708 --> 00:01:46.971
Test these decisions across the entire

36
00:01:46.971 --> 00:01:49.140
lifecycle, including failures and cleanup.

37
00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:51.781
Never let an uploaded file define its

38
00:01:51.781 --> 00:01:54.893
own trust, destination, execution context,
or authority.

39
00:01:54.893 --> 00:01:57.911
The application owns those decisions from
the first

40
00:01:57.911 --> 00:02:00.740
byte received to the last download served.

